<title>CHILE: Chile May copper exports fall to $570.5 million.</title>
<headline>Chile May copper exports fall to $570.5 million.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean copper exports fell slightly in May to $570.5 million from $585.6 million in the same month last year as the result of lower international copper prices, said the Central Bank in its fortnightly report.</p>
<p>The five percent fall in prices counteracted a rise in export volumes over the year, it said.  </p>
<p>The following are details of Chile's mining exports in May.</p>
<p> METAL			   May 1997	    May 1996</p>
<p> Copper			  570.5		 585.6</p>
<p> Iron			     14.0		  15.9</p>
<p> Salitre and iodine	   12.0		  18.8</p>
<p> Silver			    8.6		  11.2</p>
<p> Molybdenum		     21.1		  16.1</p>
<p> Lithium carbonate	     4.0		   4.8</p>
<p> Metallic gold and dore     35.0		  36.7</p>
<p> Gold mineral		    4.1		   5.7</p>
<p> Others			   11.2		   6.0</p>
<p> TOTAL			   680.5		 700.8</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures are in millions of dollars.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
